config CRUX_CLI_CONSOLE
    bool "Crux serial console start (Experimental)"
    depends on CRUX_CLI && CRUX_ACCESS
    help
      Experimental tier (ADR-0001 Decision 4): the symbol, and what it builds, may change in any
      release, and the release notes list the change. Off by default, and nothing changes in an
      image that leaves it off.

      Links the serial console with its login and first-account setup into the image, with the
      provider of the command line's event port over the security events. The module defines the
      composition target crux::cli_zephyr for <crux/cli_zephyr.h> (Experimental), which declares
      crux_cli_serial_start(): a composition interface, not a portable usage target. The console
      owns the UART that the devicetree alias crux-serial0 names, so no Zephyr console, log
      backend or shell may use it. The application passes its command tables to crux_cli_init()
      first. See docs/cli-contract.md.

